# Text is LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. Tools, tests and patches read and
# compare files byte for byte, and a script with CRLF does not run under sh. Git detects text from content; the
# binary formats are listed so that a file of one is never mistaken for text.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Terminal captures (lib/vterm/tests/captures): a program's output to a terminal and to a pipe, recorded byte for byte.
# They are binary so that git keeps their CRs and escape sequences unchanged.
*.tty binary
*.pipe binary
